course: dictionary
lesson: 6386
title: Multiples
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A multiple is what you get when you multiply a number by a whole number (1, 2, 3, 4 and so on). 6, 9 and 12 are multiples of 3, because 3 × 2 = 6, 3 × 3 = 9 and 3 × 4 = 12.
explain: Read the words around a word to find its meaning. «Check the multiples of the larger time one by one.» The clues are "check" and "larger time", so you list the times table of the bigger number and look for the answer you need.
explain: Multiple can also be an adjective, meaning many. «Multiple choice» means a test with many answers to pick from, and «multiple times» means many times.
fact: A multiple of a number is what you get when you multiply it by a whole number.
fact: «Multiples of 8 are 8, 16, 24 …» The multiples of 8 are the numbers in the 8 times table.
fact: A common multiple is a number that is a multiple of two or more numbers.
fact: The lowest common multiple is the smallest number that is a multiple of both numbers.
fact: As an adjective, «multiple» means many, as in «multiple choice».
exercise: Which of these is a multiple of 3? | 10 | *12 | 5 | 7
exercise: «Buses every 6 and every 8 minutes» meet again after how many minutes? Find the first number that is a multiple of both 6 and 8. | *24 | 12 | 30 | 16
exercise: In «multiple choice», what does multiple mean? | Hidden | *Many | Very small | One only
test: Which number is NOT a multiple of 4? | 16 | 8 | 20 | *18
test: What are the first three multiples of 5? | *5, 10, 15 | 1, 2, 3 | 2, 4, 6 | 50, 100, 150
exam: The sentence says «multiples of 10, such as 20 and 40, but not 15 or 35.» Which number is a multiple of 10? | 45 | *40 | 35 | 15
